    <briefdescription>
<para>Logical NOT comparator struct template. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Derived from <computeroutput><ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1unary__op" kindref="compound">unary_op</ref></computeroutput>, this struct negates a single sub-expression, enabling test writers to assert that a condition does not hold. The negation result is computed at construction time, ensuring consistent reporting throughout the assertion framework.</para>
<para>The sub-expression is not copied: a temporary is moved into the comparator, and a named one is referred to (see <computeroutput><ref refid="namespacemicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1a85cd019d0861a4b6d62c3424f4a8931d" kindref="member">stored_operand_t</ref></computeroutput>).</para>
<para>There is no deduction guide: with a single argument that is itself a <computeroutput><ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1not__op" kindref="compound">not_op</ref></computeroutput>, the class template argument deduction prefers the copy deduction candidate, so <computeroutput><ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1not__op" kindref="compound">not_op</ref>{ inner }</computeroutput> would copy <computeroutput>inner</computeroutput> instead of negating it. Name the template argument instead, as <computeroutput><ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1not__op" kindref="compound">not_op</ref>&lt;<ref refid="namespacemicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1a85cd019d0861a4b6d62c3424f4a8931d" kindref="member">stored_operand_t</ref>&lt;T&gt;&gt;{ t }</computeroutput>.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The type of the stored sub-expression, either its type, or a <computeroutput>const</computeroutput> reference to it. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
